  "answer_text": "Here is an overview of the **Georgia Motor Vehicle Division (MVD) Tag Renewal portal** at **mvd.dor.ga.gov/tags/index.aspx**:\n\n---\n\n## \ud83d\ude97 Georgia MVD \u2013 Tag Renewal Portal\n\nThis is the **official online tag (vehicle registration) renewal website** for the State of Georgia, operated by the **Georgia Department of Revenue (DOR)**.\n\n### What You Can Do There:\n\nGeorgia MVD offers online applications and information regarding **tag renewals, license plates, titles, dealer registrations, and commercial vehicles**.\n\nKey features of the portal include:\n\n- **Renew your vehicle tag/registration online**\n- **Obtain/Retrieve a RIN** (Renewal Identification Number) by entering your plate number, name, and address.\n- A **RIN** is a **12-digit number** necessary for completing online renewals.\n- **Request services** without re-entering VINs, license plates, or driver's license numbers each time, and quickly access vehicles associated with your driver's license.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udccb Things to Know Before Renewing Online:\n\n- If the **address on your Renewal Notice is not correct**, do not renew online. You must also present your **driver's license or Georgia ID** to renew.\n- After vehicle registration, you will receive a **license plate with a decal** which must be **renewed each year**.\n- Georgia offers **hundreds of specialty plate designs** to choose from, including veterans, colleges, special interest groups, and more.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udcde Contact & Verification:\n\n- The telephone number for MVD is **(855) 406-5221**.\n- Call **1-800-GEORGIA** to verify that a website is an official website of the State of Georgia.\n\n---\n\n> \ud83d\udd17 You can visit the portal directly at: **[mvd.dor.ga.gov/tags/index.aspx](https://mvd.dor.ga.gov/tags/index.aspx)**\n\nWould you like help with a specific task, such as renewing your tag or finding your local tag office?",
